{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/7488-threats-unknown-and-other-such-strangeness","id":7488,"title":"'Threats Unknown' and Other Such Strangeness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-10T10:50:32-08:00","id":7488,"title":"'Threats Unknown' and Other Such Strangeness","content":"There's some talk about a Hunter book being pitched somewhere down the line, after The Something About Monsters Comes Out, that covers antagonists and phenomena that don't fit any of the main gamelines (Vampires, Werewolves, Mages, the Reanimated, Changelings, Ghosts/Sin-Eaters, Mummies, and God-Machine Demons). While such a thing is at this point an idea of an idea, I'd like to open up this thread to gauge interest and maybe inspire the Onyx Path writers a bit.<br /> <br /> What would you want to see in an 'assorted weird things' book?<br /> <br /> I'm hoping for more on Intersitial Terrain, as described in the Horror Recognition Guide Story &quot;Ten Photographs.&quot; The idea of overlapping realities that aren't explicitly the Hedge or anything else familiar (like the weird meat-machine Philadelphia) sounds fascinating, and allows for all sorts of fun stuff; everything from slightly different realities to wherever the USS Eldridge went on that fateful October day.<br /> <br /> I'd also like to see some info on aliens and vague government mystery (I think the Horror Recognition Guide had a story on this as well?), if only to feed my infinite hunger for 90s-style conspiracy fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T11:10:38-08:00","id":7509,"title":"","content":"I would very much like one; I'd recommend reading Unkown Armies for inspiration.<br /> <br /> It would also be a good way to introduce low powered threats. The sort of things where you can run combats for Tier 1 / 2 hunters without needing to use a ton of dirty tricks to even the odds. Instead use dirty tricks to get a solid advantage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T11:26:29-08:00","id":7522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/7488-threats-unknown-and-other-such-strangeness?p=7509#post7509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would very much like one; I'd recommend reading Unkown Armies for inspiration.<br /> <br /> It would also be a good way to introduce low powered threats. The sort of things where you can run combats for Tier 1 / 2 hunters without needing to use a ton of dirty tricks to even the odds. Instead use dirty tricks to get a solid advantage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny you should mention it; one of my followers tipped me off to UA yesterday, and I'm quite enjoying the read.<br /> <br /> Low-Tier threats and more &quot;mysteries&quot; than outright monsters would be very helpful. Hell, a big bunch of rumors would be a lot of fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T12:25:48-08:00","id":7563,"title":"","content":"More looking at the conspiracies from the point of view of a lower-tier hunter, especially when gauging whether or not they're on the same fight. Aliens and extra-dimensional beings works too, since those are relatively absent in WoD.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't mind an entire book about cryptids and strange animals, but that sounds more like a vanilla WoD book considering a lot of those are more local legends than worldwide phenomena.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T13:07:51-08:00","id":7597,"title":"","content":"Looking at the conspiracies from a low tier hunter would be interesting, but I think it would have to be done from the perspective of trying to annoy them enough that they leave but not enough them so much that they send a whole army to crush you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T13:12:01-08:00","id":7603,"title":"","content":"Something important not necessarily related; advice on multi-Compact or multi-Conspiracy cells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T13:29:38-08:00","id":7625,"title":"","content":"You don't need a book for that. In fact one word would be enough: &quot;Avoid&quot;.<br /> <br /> Ok, I'm significantly exadurating for effect. However each compact / conspiracy is basically a different game. You can definitely do it, however it is basically crossover in my opinion and crossover always dilutes the themes of the individual gamelines, and usually requires some furious hand-waving. Why isn't the VASCU guy reporting the Ascending One for connections to the drug trade? Why doesn't the Ageis Kai Doru agent kill the MM priest for Witchcraft? It's hard to get the Union's feeling of ignorant hunters who get by on grit and community spirit if your cellmate is a Loyalist with ye olde tomes of accurate knowledge<br /> <br /> So IMO, any crossover section would have to talk more how you create new themes to replace the diluted themes of individual groups than just being a big list of excuses to tell the brass. That said, I think that what's much more important than a crossover section is really solid rules going in depth in one group. Everything form the basics - how to ask for backup - to entire games spent dealing with internal matters. (I'm working on a fanbook called Cults where I hope to address some of those issues)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T17:49:03-08:00","id":7767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/7488-threats-unknown-and-other-such-strangeness#post7488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm hoping for more on Intersitial Terrain, as described in the Horror Recognition Guide Story &quot;Ten Photographs.&quot; The idea of overlapping realities that aren't explicitly the Hedge or anything else familiar (like the weird meat-machine Philadelphia) sounds fascinating, and allows for all sorts of fun stuff; everything from slightly different realities to wherever the USS Eldridge went on that fateful October day.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a good-sized section on the phenomenon in Shadows of the U.K., if that counts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T08:05:05-08:00","id":8089,"title":"","content":"I can see two possible formats for this book.*<br /> <br /> One is based on the Night Horrors format, with relatively short sections on each beasty. But like Wicked Dead, it could have a longer section for a more elaborate take on a creature. The first and second sections could be an assortment of monsters, the third a longer treatments of a specific one- Ghouls from the corebook's fiction being the most obvious choice. <br /> <br /> The other format is like Monstrous Basterds; i.e., more in-depth treatments but a smaller number overall, modeled on Witch Finders/Night Stalkers/Spirit Slayers. I can see expanding on Interstitial Terrain (&quot;threats from the universe next door&quot;), Ghouls and the Djinn (from Compacts &amp; Conspiracies).<br /> <br /> *Or two books! Or three. A Hunter Night Horrors book, a core mortals Night Horrors book, and then a Hunter Threats Unknown book. <br /> <br /> The mortals/demons-oriented Night Horrors book could be themed around the God-Machine's &quot;rivals.&quot; The God-Machines of neighboring universes, viral deities infecting the operating system, other malfunctions, the prototype God-Machines from the universe before this one and what they've gotten up to lately, etc.<br /> <br /> The hunter-oriented Night Horrors book could be themed around stuff that resembles, but isn't, the other game lines. One-off vampires, shapeshifters, zombies, ghouls, etc. Stuff with specific folkloric backing and weaknesses to support a monster-of-the-week Hunter game. <br /> <br /> Then Threats Unknown for Hunter material intended for &quot;deeper&quot; effects on the wider world of darkness. You consult Night Horrors: Monster Safari when you're killing the one and only specimen of its type in the world. You consult Threats Unknown when you want to do a campaign opposing an invasion by body-snatching aliens from a dark future, or a cannibal ghoul people-smuggling/eating ring out of Russia.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T08:16:08-08:00","id":8102,"title":"","content":"I'd go for a Night Horrors style book. But maybe three times as many creatures and 1/3 the wordcount for each. Rather than a full background for each monster, a stat block, new dread powers if necessary and storytelling section.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/7488-threats-unknown-and-other-such-strangeness?p=8089#post8089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IThe mortals/demons-oriented Night Horrors book could be themed around the God-Machine's &quot;rivals.&quot; The God-Machines of neighboring universes, viral deities infecting the operating system, other malfunctions, the prototype God-Machines from the universe before this one and what they've gotten up to lately, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems more like a core book than a hunter book, but damn if that's not a good idea!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T12:44:07-08:00","id":8305,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m going to have to see what <b>Remains</b> does in terms of its \u201chow to build a monster\u201d chapter; depending on how it\u2019s done, there may be little for a <b>Threats Unknown</b> to do other than to be a <b>Night Horrors</b>-style assorted bestiary for <b>Hunter</b>. If <b>Remains</b> gets too focused on just building reanimated, faeries, mediums, mummies, and demons, then I could see <b>Threats Unknown</b> expanding on it to cover guidelines for building other kinds of monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T15:52:57-08:00","id":8428,"title":"","content":"Some threats that, while clearly supernatural, cannot be attributed to the other splats. So a book of things where people can't say 'Oh that's an Abyssal spirit' or 'Probably a geist.'<br /> <br /> I'd love some individual examples, like in the Night Horrors line (seriously my favorite group of books).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T04:29:35-08:00","id":8718,"title":"","content":"Something Cthulu-esque might be cool...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1023-marz-blaque","name":"Marz Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1023_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T06:28:38-08:00","id":8757,"title":"","content":"I'd be very interested in this! Probably more even then those about major gamelines interpreted through hunter. UFOs, Cthulhu stuff, various kinds of demons, and I hope stuff on Gods/Mythology could fit! It would be cool to have a conspiracy based around something not of a major Gameline!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T07:45:32-08:00","id":8798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Professor Phobos:</b> The other format is like Monstrous Basterds; i.e., more in-depth treatments but a smaller number overall, modeled on Witch Finders/Night Stalkers/Spirit Slayers. I can see expanding on Interstitial Terrain (&quot;threats from the universe next door&quot;), Ghouls and the Djinn (from Compacts &amp; Conspiracies). </div> </div> </div>I'd prefer this approach. And all three of those are good.<br /> <br /> Another that comes to mind is one of the most oft-fanmade/called-for additions, the Reckoning Imbued. It might seem strange to count them as monsters, but they are - unlike tier 3 hunters - unabiguously powered and guided by external supernatural forces (and &quot;they're still human&quot; is already something that can be applied to witches, so it's not really a get-out here).<br /> <br /> They're supernaturally-powered individuals who seem driven to destroy other things like them. Are they allies? Another third tier group in effect? Or monsters who are just taking on the competition? (And are the first and third necessarily exclusive)?<br /> <br /> Additionally, one of the themes of Reckoning was that the Imbued were a new phenomenon. Keeping that aspect adds an element to hunters' responses to them that's not present in the existing monsters, or in other ideas for TU.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T13:44:01-08:00","id":13590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/7488-threats-unknown-and-other-such-strangeness?p=8428#post8428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some threats that, while clearly supernatural, cannot be attributed to the other splats. So a book of things where people can't say 'Oh that's an Abyssal spirit' or 'Probably a geist.'</div> </div> </div> </div>A million trillion bazillion times this. This would be AWESOME<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":568,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/568-viperion","user":"Viperion","date":". 11-18-2013, 04:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/568-viperion","name":"Viperion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar568_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}